{\pard\ql\fs20 Standard errors in parentheses\par}
{\pard\ql\fs20 Country and year fixed effects are included in all models, and standard errors are clustered by country.\par}
{\pard\ql\fs20 Lags cover one- and two-year horizons.\par}
{\pard\ql\fs20 The dependent variable is climate discourse in Models (1) and (4), climate policy intensity in Model (2), and climate readiness in Model (3).\par}
{\pard\ql\fs20 Panel A reports fixed-effects estimates; Panel B reports joint Wald block-exogeneity test p-values.\par}
{\pard\ql\fs20 Models (2) and (3) are interpreted as reverse-ordering diagnostics, not as evidence that central bank communication causes national climate policy or country-level readiness.\par}
{\pard\ql\fs20 Model (4) adds L1(DV) to account for persistence.\par}
{\pard\ql\fs20 The estimates are interpreted as Granger-style predictive associations rather than causal Granger tests.\par}
{\pard\ql\fs20 *** p<0.01, ** p<0.05, * p<0.10.\par}
